<h1>TActiveDropDownList</h1>
<com:SinceVersion Version="3.1" />
<com:DocLink ClassPath="Prado.Web.UI.ActiveControls.TActiveDropDownList" />

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TActiveDropDownList</tt> is the active counterpart to the original <tt>TDropDownList</tt> control.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
The <tt>AutoPostBack</tt> property is set to true by default.
Thus, when the drop down list selection is changed the <tt>OnCallback</tt> event is
raised after <tt>OnSelectedIndexChanged</tt> event.
</p>

<h2>What updates during a callback</h2>

<p class="block-content">
The selection can be changed from the server. Assigning <tt>SelectedIndex</tt>,
<tt>SelectedIndices</tt>, <tt>SelectedValue</tt>, or <tt>SelectedValues</tt> moves the
selection in the browser, subject to <a href="?page=ActiveControls.Introduction#ClientSideUpdates">the five conditions for a client-side update</a>. A list with a prompt item counts
the prompt outside the index, in the same way a postback does.
</p>

<h2>Changing the items</h2>

<p class="block-content">
<tt>TActiveDropDownList</tt> is one of two controls in this chapter whose
<tt>Items</tt> collection can be rebuilt during a callback, the other being
<a href="?page=ActiveControls.ActiveListBox">TActiveListBox</a>. Adding, removing, or
rebinding items sends the new option list to the browser, so a handler can repopulate one
list from the choice made in another.
</p>

<p class="block-content">
Please refer to the original documentation of <a href="?page=Controls.List">TDropDownList</a> for usage.
</p>

